{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1432908-a-vulture-s-eye-tell-tale-heart-inspiration","id":1432908,"title":"A Vulture's Eye [Tell Tale Heart Inspiration]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-21T06:39:48-08:00","id":1432908,"title":"A Vulture's Eye [Tell Tale Heart Inspiration]","content":"You are being watched.<br /> <br /> Most people do not know it. Most people can't know it. For the vast majority of humans, the world is just that- a world, a plain reality which slowly grinds their body and soul through each and passing day. They don't notice it. They don't care about it. Their senses are just not... acute enough. They can only see in the brightest light and hear the loudest of sounds. For them, there is nothing weird about the world- and if they notice by any chance that there is something slithering in the shadows, they lie to themselves and keep on moving. The slightest of veils is enough for them to not notice- but not you. You are different. You can see it. You can hear it. It is there, in plain sight- but they can't notice. It's absurd! How can they just ignore it? How can't they see it? They must have seen it. They ignore it just to mock you. They are a part of it. It's all coming together. You are not crazy- the world is. Something must be done. You must stop seeing it. You must bring an end to it. You can't keep bearing it watching you. All you have to do, is taking the knife and put an end to it. It's not that difficult. It will soon all be over.<br /> <br /> No one needs to know. They won't notice, anyway. Soon it will all be over.<br /> <br /> And then, you will no longer have to see that damn vulture eye.<br /> <br /> The Shadow is strange. Even the Uratha will admit it- a spiritual land which constantly hovers right next to you, yet most people can't touch it. It is a world where concepts take form, where hunger is the only constant and where hierarchy and renown are the equivalent for the laws of physics. Yet, while it is separate from the Flesh, <i>Hisil</i> is strongly tied to it- for the Shadow influence the Flesh, while the Flesh attracts the Shadow. It is a constant feedback loop, where one feed the other and no one knows who is the chickens and who is the egg. Was it the car accident which started to draw spirits of misfortune to that person, or where there the spirits which caused the accident? Did those marriage created the love spirit, or did the spirit influenced them to marry so it could feed on their love? And that before we start talking about things which are truly weird, like the remains of long dead gods which wear human bodies like clothes, or the ever changing <i>idigam</i> which break any boundary and cross any limit. The Shadow is there, and it is watching, and it is hungry, yet for most people there is nothing there- they can't feel the whispers on their neck, they can see the ethereal dance of spirits, they can't hear the faint screams of <i>Hisil</i>'s denizens as they are hunted down by their brethren. The Shadow is watching you, and unless something really bad would happen, you will never know it.<br /> <br /> Until one day, something bad happens. You see that something is watching you, and that it knows that you are watching it.<br /> <br /> And then, the mind breaks, and all hell breaks loose.<br /> <br /> The so called &quot;Vulture Eye Syndrome&quot; is something talked about among some occultist circles- as it is a rare phenomenon, yet it occurs enough times for it to gain its own name. Those Bone Shadows which investigated the Syndrome claim it to be a very strange form of a Spirit Ridden- one which, for some reason, does not influence the one that it rides, but someone around them. It is some kind of a projection, they say- the spirit behind it settles around someone, yet the effects of the possession are being transferred to someone else, slowly driving them mad until they murder the carrier of the spirit. Almost always, the one who suffer from the Syndrome is someone close to the Ridden, and usually the closer they are, the sooner they will be driven mad. Now, many occultists argue that the Syndrome is not, actually, a syndrome- it is just paranoia which starts when someone notice that a person close to them start to act weird due to spiritual possession. There is nothing strange about it- after all, people should notice when their loved one acts weird, and add to it the spirit acting like a spirit, it is little wonder that some people will try to kill those which are Urged by the spirits. After all, people don't want to know what lurks in the darkness, and when it comes to their doorsteps, many of them could indeed lose their minds because of it.<br /> <br /> There is, however, one problem with that explanation.<br /> <br /> The titular &quot;Vulture's Eye&quot;.<br /> <br /> It is common for everyone who suffers from the Syndrome. It all starts when, during one bright day, something bad happens- maybe they lost their job, maybe they fell down the stairs, maybe something bad happened to someone they care about. Maybe they just had a bad day- nothing too extraordinary. However, after that event, those people have stumbled upon someone they know, be it some distant friend or their significant other. And while they happy to meet them, they notice something strange about them. One of their eyes is... weird. It's blue, pale blue. Almost avian in nature, like some kind of a raptor... a vulture. It watches them with a cruel guise. It mocks them. It judges them. That eye is evil, plain and simple- but they can't do anything. They can't acknowledge that it exists. It is there, and no one knows it is there but them. They are being watched, and they will always be watched- as long as the damn eye will stay open.<br /> <br /> And then they leave, and all they could think about is that pale blue vulture eye.<br /> <br /> While you may think that the easiest thing to do is to talk about the eye, they can't do it- doing so will acknowledge the eye's existence, will acknowledge that this situation is real. Instead, they try to ignore it- suck it up and ignore the watchful sight of the eye. But they can't- for they know that the eye is watching them. Every time they look on the carrier's face, they see the eye. Every time they look at their pictures, the eye is there. Every time time they look in the mirror, the eye is watching in the corners. The eye is there in the shards of broken glass. The eye is there at the edge of their sight. The eye is there in their dreams. The eye is there in the middle of the sky- pale blue, cruel and awful. The eye is there- and no one knows it. No one notice it. Only they know about the eye, and only they can bring an end to it.<br /> <br /> And so, they resolve to murder.<br /> <br /> How fast the victim will fall to the act depends on their own mental integrity- some will; try and hold the paranoia at bay, while others will simply skydive into the bottom, ending the act as fast as they can. However, while under the influence of the eye, the victim would start growing closer to the spiritual world- as if the sight of an ever watching eye is not enough, their sight would start penetrating into the Twilight, into the Gauntlet. They'll start hearing things from across the veil, or feel the touch of spiritual entities. While the eye would surely drive them into insanity on its own, the sudden closeness to the Shadow accelerates it, driving their mental fortitude and feeding their paranoia until their only choice is to end it all and make the eye stop watching them.<br /> <br /> So they kill the person. The murder to eye. That's should be the end, isn't it?<br /> <br /> But it isn't. It's not over, not yet.<br /> <br /> The eye is still watching.<br /> <br /> It is a weird experience, they would say- the act is done, they should finally sleep in peace, but they can't. The eye is still there. It is still watching. It slowly eats in their minds- and after they look in the mirror they see why. The eye is there, in their own sockets, mocking them for whatever they did. Everything they did was in vain. Everyone would know about their actions. Everyone would see what they did. Everyone know that they are all messed up inside, and that there is nothing they can do to hide it. The can try, but eventually they'll see it- they must see it! It's in there, in their face! No one could ignore it now. They all are just acting ignorant, waiting for them to break down, enjoying their misery. The only thing that's left is to confess, to stop that suffering, to stop that mocking. Force them to acknowledge that this vulture eye is watching! They must see it, right? Right?<br /> <br /> They are sane. Every action they did was sane. Just please, acknowledge it. Let them know that you are seeing it.<br /> <br /> But you can't see it. There is nothing there. And that's a good thing.<br /> <br /> Because only when you'll see it, it will see you.<br /> <br /> Until then, it would be watching.<br /> <br /> <b><u>System</u></b><br /> <br /> People who suffer from the Vulture Eye Syndrome develop it after suffering from a Breaking Point while in an area which is close to the Shadow, after which they meet someone they know in the later Scene. When they do, they need to roll their Composure + Resolve in order to resist the influence of the cause behind the Syndrome. Developing the Syndrome, however, is not limited to mortals- monsters, such as werewolves, could also develop it, even though that they also add their Supernatural Tolerance trait to the roll. If the person they meet is especially close to the victim, such as being their Touchstone, they suffer from a -2 modifier to the resistance roll. In a case of a failure, they would start seeing the Eye- only in the face of the carrier, at first, yet slowly it would show up everywhere, causing them to become more and more obsessives towards making it to stop watching them, at any price it will take.<br /> <br /> After developing the Syndrome, the victim immediately develops the Spooked Condition, which later turns into the Obsessives Condition towards the victim, which can not be resolved. Also, the victim discovers that they can't speak about the eye- simply mentioning its existence requires a Composure + Resolve roll, which is penalized by 10 - Integrity (or equivalent). After a number of days which is equal to the Integrity (or equivalent) score, they would also start seeing and hearing into the Twilight even if they usually can't. They can't however, control it- and if the victim generally have control over it, they need to roll Composure + Resolve every time they try to maintain it. By the end of this duration, the victim would also develop the Delusional Condition which can't be resolved.<br /> <br /> After the victim develops their spiritual senses, they sight of the eye starts to rapidly erode their minds. For every number of days equal to their Integrity equivalent days, they need to roll for a Breaking Point, and they become clearly aware that as long as they eye is watching they can not truly rest. For mortals, when they reach an Integrity of 4, their murderous urges start taking control, granting them a Ripper Undertaking of their choosing even though they don't feel compelled to murder anyone beside the eye's carrier. While having this score or lower, the victim discovers that becoming so close to the Shadow have also affected their presence- giving them a modifier equal to 10 - Integrity in order to conceal their presence. Also at this point, the victim discover themselves ever more motivated to put an end to the accursed eye- forcing them to roll Composure + Resolve (+ Supernatural Tolerance) in order to resist killing the target when they have the chance. That roll is too penalized by 10 - Integrity.<br /> <br /> While the wait to the murder is eroding, once the act is done their first feeling is a form of relief. After the act, the Obsessives Condition is being resolved, and they no longer suffer from the forced Breaking Points or the need to kill, as well as the compulsion to not speak about the eye (they do, however, retain the other features of the Syndrome). This, however, is a short lived relief- as the Syndrome is not solved by the murder, only changes. A Scene after the act, the victim will develop a new persistent Obsessives Condition- one towards the murder itself, instead of the dead carrier. They also discover that where once they couldn't speak about the horror, now they just can't shut up about it- talking about the act of the murder up to its finest details every time that it is mentioned now requires a Composure + Resolve roll. Now, the eye also starts showing up everywhere, using the victim as its focus. They are no longer, however, compelled to kill- but at this point the madness runs so deep and their Integrity is so low, that it is only a matter of time before they'll become true slashers, haunted by a cruel, vulture eye.<br /> <br /> Note- in the case of werewolves which suffer from the Syndrome, the Breaking Points are always towards Spirit. Also, while it is possible to werewolves to notice some kind of spiritual influence around the victim and the carrier, they generally can't find the exact cause for the Syndrome, as there doesn't seem to be any spirit which directly rides the flesh of the carrier or urges the victim. A few, however, have managed to glean some information about the source of the Syndrome by asking old spirits or lunes, or by using some means to scry after the thing behind the phenomenon. All that they managed to gain, however, is the knowledge that the thing behind it is something ancient and cruel, as well as the clear image of a pale blue avian eye which watches through the cracks of broken glass. Whatever the meaning behind this is currently unknown.<br /> <br /> [So blame OSP Red for this. I've just heard her reading the poem for the first time and the first thing which came into my mind was &quot;damn it, this must be tied to Bird in some way!&quot;, so here you have it. Hope you like it]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}